<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The recording proxy, as a launchd agent.

  The proxy is the only way to capture opencode's system prompt and tool
  schemas: they are baked into the opencode binary and are not exposed by
  ``opencode debug agent``, so the request itself is the ground truth.

  A launchd agent rather than a shell background job, because the full
  re-annotation runs for days: a process started from a tool call dies with
  it, and a proxy that is down makes every trial in flight fail.

  Install and start it with::

      # 1. put your own paths in: the repository, and the run root
      sed -i '' "s|/path/to/harness-rsi|$PWD|g; s|/path/to/rsi-harbor|$HOME/.rsi-harbor|g" \
          opencode_sft/launchd/com.rsi.opencode.proxy.plist
      # 2. install it
      cp opencode_sft/launchd/com.rsi.opencode.proxy.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
      launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.rsi.opencode.proxy.plist

  The paths in this file are **placeholders**: a launchd agent needs absolute
  paths, and a repository cannot know where it was cloned to.

  **The pipeline does not need this agent.**  ``common/run_all_stages.sh``
  starts the proxy itself, on ``PROXY_PORT`` (8910 by default), and the two
  opencode streams talk to that one.  This plist is for the case where the
  proxy has to be up on its own -- for instance while a single trial is being
  captured by hand.

  The port below is deliberately **not** 8910: the orchestrator's proxy owns
  that port, and two proxies appending to the same request log would
  interleave their writes.  Give this one its own port and its own log.

  The request log lives under the run root, not in /private/tmp: the host
  rebooted once during the pilot and took the whole /private/tmp tree with it,
  which cost the captured system prompts and tool schemas of every trial that
  had run so far.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.rsi.opencode.proxy</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/path/to/harness-rsi/.venv312/bin/python</string>
    <string>/path/to/harness-rsi/common/record_proxy.py</string>
    <string>--host</string>
    <string>0.0.0.0</string>
    <string>--port</string>
    <string>8899</string>
    <string>--upstream</string>
    <string>http://YOUR-ENDPOINT:PORT/v1</string>
    <string>--out</string>
    <string>/path/to/rsi-harbor/logs/oc-requests-standalone.jsonl</string>
    <string>--compact</string>
    <string>--dedupe</string>
    <string>--blob-dir</string>
    <string>/path/to/rsi-harbor/logs/oc-blobs-standalone</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/path/to/harness-rsi</string>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/path/to/rsi-harbor/logs/oc-proxy.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/path/to/rsi-harbor/logs/oc-proxy.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
